     "result_text_tail": "030 within the board's limits.** Option A reaches about $26M. The deck recommends keeping the limits and moving the $40M milestone to about 2032.\n- **The deck also corrects three items circulated to the board.** The $5.2B trade-press figure includes makeup and hair care. The 1.3\u00d7 \"retail halo\" on Amazon sales rests on a correlation that may run the other way. The CEO's 15% awareness gate for adding retail is too low; the evidence points to 20%.\n\n**Choices I made in your absence** (all listed on the last slide so the board can confirm them):\n1. **The $40M target:** I treated it as a direction. The cash cap, payback, margin floor and one-launch limit are treated as binding.\n2. **Awareness:** I used 4% (all facial-skincare buyers) because that is the base the retail sell-through table uses. The 9% figure among K-beauty buyers gives the same conclusion.\n3. **Main stress case:** 32% ad cost, because Option A's revenue path matches the benchmark brands.\n4. **Tariff stress:** a 25% duty applied to all four years.\n5. **Proposals for the board:** a $4M cash limit before the decision comes back to the board, and the retail gates: 20% awareness, $20M of Amazon sales and a test of about 300 doors. These are my numbers, not the board's.\n6. **Japan's working capital:** left out, because the pack doesn't give it.\n7. **After 2030:** I extended Option A at +25% a year, for illustration only.\n\nThe model and the deck-building scripts are in `./build/` if you want to rerun with different inputs."
